## How GreenOnion Compares to Other AI Listing Tools

| Tool | Compliance focus | Scoring system | Speed | Pricing |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **GreenOnion** | ✅ Yes (policy-aware) | ⚠️ Binary (compliant/incompliant) | 60s claim | [PENDING] |
| **Picjam** | ⚠️ Partial (best practices) | ✅ Yes (0-100 score) | Slower (iterative) | [PENDING] |
| ChatGPT custom instructions | ❌ No | ❌ No | 30-60s (depends on prompt) | $20/mo |
| Jasper | ❌ No | ❌ No | 60-90s | $49/mo |
| Copy.ai | ❌ No | ❌ No | 60-90s | $36/mo |

The key insight: **GreenOnion and Picjam take different angles on the same problem.** GreenOnion is compliance-first: it tells you whether your listing is acceptable. Picjam is scoring-first: it tells you how good your listing is on a 0-100 scale. For different merchant segments, one or the other is more useful.

## Use Cases: When to Pick GreenOnion

Based on our test, GreenOnion is the better choice for:
- **New sellers on Amazon** who don't know all the policy rules yet
- **Multi-platform sellers** who need consistent compliance across 3-4 channels
- **Bulk listing** scenarios where you have 100+ products to publish quickly
- **Account safety focus** sellers who've been suspended before and need bulletproof listings

GreenOnion is probably NOT the best choice for:
- **Conversion optimization focus** (use Picjam instead)
- **A+ Content generation** (neither does this well; you need Jasper or a designer)
- **Brand voice consistency** (GreenOnion's outputs feel more generic than Picjam's)

